  {
    "id": "saint-matthew-the-apostle",
    "day": "November 16",
    "name": "Saint Matthew the Apostle",
    "description": "STRUCTURALLY MOVABLE, not an unresearched gap: per the authoritative account of the East Syriac liturgical year (Beth Kokheh, 'The Ecclesiastical Liturgical Year for the Church of the East'), this figure is commemorated only as the Four Evangelists, Third Friday of the pre-Fast cycle -- a date that shifts every year with the Denkha season length, the same cycle already computed by getPreFastSundayFoldSchedule() in js/calendar-east-syriac.js (built 2026-08-30, deliberately unwired). No fixed Gregorian date exists for this commemoration in this tradition; sourcing it properly needs that movable-date system wired into Layer 3 display, not a fixed month/day entry like the rest of this file.",
    "type": "apostle",
    "tags": [
      "EOR",
      "LAT",
      "OOR"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "mar-gregory-the-wonderworker",
    "day": "November 17",
    "name": "Mar Gregory the Wonderworker",
    "description": "CHECKED 2026-08-31, tradition mismatch found: Gregory Thaumaturgus (c.213-270), Bishop of Neocaesarea, 'the Wonder-worker.' His own Wikipedia infobox lists 'Venerated in: Catholic Church, Eastern Orthodox Church, Oriental Orthodoxy' -- the Church of the East is not among the traditions listed. Same pattern already found for saint-ahudemmeh, mar-behnam-and-sarah, and virgin-martyr-febronia-of-nisibis. Not this session's call to resolve (the allowlist is a separate, already-audited March 2026 artifact); flagged for that allowlist's own future review.",
    "type": "saint",
    "tags": []
  },
